## What I did differently, and why

**One `@future` call per trigger execution instead of one per unique account.**

The instructions said "one future call per opportunity," but with 200-opportunity CPQ batches across ~40 unique accounts that is 40 separate `@future` invocations. The `@future` governor limit is **50 per transaction**, so this works but leaves almost no headroom, and each invocation runs its own SOQL + DML for a single account.

I changed `recalculate` to accept `List<Id> accountIds` so the trigger fires **exactly one** `@future` call per DML batch. Inside that call all accounts are processed with **one SOQL and one DML**, which is bulk-safe and well under every governor limit. This also eliminates the risk of the limit being exceeded if a single trigger execution touches more than 50 unique accounts.

