The `UserRecordAccess` object records the *computed* access each user has to each record, folding in object/field perms, ownership, OWD, sharing rules, role hierarchy, and View All/Modify All. It is unindexed unless you filter by `UserId` (which, combined with `RecordId`, uses its composite index), so the query must always pin `UserId = runningUser` and `HasEditAccess = true`. Since an `IN` bind collection should stay well under the documented limits, we chunk the IDs (500 → 4 SOQL for the worst case of 2,000, comfortably below the 20-query cap) and intersect the returned `RecordId`s with the input. Records absent from `UserRecordAccess` or flagged read-only are naturally excluded, which is exactly "cannot edit."

File: force-app/main/default/classes/RecordAccessService.cls
```apex
/**
 * Resolves, for the running user, which of a set of record Ids are actually editable.
 * Uses the UserRecordAccess system object (which already accounts for object/field
 * permissions, ownership, OWD, sharing rules, the role hierarchy and View All /
 * Modify All). Query is filtered on UserId + RecordId so it leverages the composite
 * index, and HasEditAccess = true so only editable records are returned.
 *
 * @param recordIds Ids to test (may span multiple objects). Up to ~2,000 per call.
 * @return the subset that the running user can edit; empty (never null) if input is null/empty.
 */
public with sharing class RecordAccessService {

    // Keep each IN clause well within SOQL bind-collection limits.
    // 2,000 / 500 = 4 SOQL queries, far under the 20-query budget.
    private static final Integer CHUNK_SIZE = 500;

    public static Set<Id> editableIds(Set<Id> recordIds) {
        Set<Id> editable = new Set<Id>();
        if (recordIds == null || recordIds.isEmpty()) {
            return editable; // contract: never return null
        }

        // De-duplicate (Set input is already unique) and drop any null entries so the
        // IN list stays clean.
        List<Id> ids = new List<Id>();
        for (Id recordId : recordIds) {
            if (recordId != null) {
                ids.add(recordId);
            }
        }
        if (ids.isEmpty()) {
            return editable;
        }

        Id runningUser = UserInfo.getUserId();

        // Chunked query: one SOQL per chunk, filtered on UserId (index) + HasEditAccess.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < ids.size(); i += CHUNK_SIZE) {
            Integer upper = Math.min(i + CHUNK_SIZE, ids.size());
            List<Id> chunk = ids.subList(i, upper);

            for (UserRecordAccess access : [
                SELECT RecordId
                FROM UserRecordAccess
                WHERE UserId = :runningUser
                  AND HasEditAccess = true
                  AND RecordId IN :chunk
            ]) {
                editable.add(access.RecordId);
            }
        }

        return editable;
    }
}
